      {
        "id": "v2-7d2ee-p11-practice-slot-2-upper-s2u-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Which two cards have the same value? Explain why.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2^6$ and $-(-2)^6$ both equal $-64$, while $(-2)^6=64$. In both, the index applies to $2$ and a minus sign is applied afterwards.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(-2)^6&=64\\\\-2^6&=-(2\\times2\\times2\\times2\\times2\\times2)\\\\&=-64\\\\-(-2)^6&=-64\\end{align*}$$\nIn $(-2)^6$ the six negative factors give a positive product. In $-2^6$ the index applies to $2$ and the minus sign comes after. In $-(-2)^6$ the bracket is evaluated first, then the minus sign is applied. The last two cards both equal $-64$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
    ]
  },
